autobyteus-web/docs/file_explorer.md:293:The File Search feature enables users to quickly find files within a workspace by typing a search query. It uses backend snapshot search strategies such as `fuzzysort` and displays results as clickable file items.
autobyteus-web/docs/file_explorer.md:470:The frontend sends a `SearchFiles` GraphQL query. Search is a request/response snapshot operation and must not start a live watcher. See [autobyteus-server-ts/docs/modules/file_explorer.md](../../autobyteus-server-ts/docs/modules/file_explorer.md) for backend implementation details including:
autobyteus-web/docs/file_explorer.md:474:- File name index refreshes from snapshot traversal instead of persistent watcher state
autobyteus-web/docs/file_explorer.md:526:Real-time file synchronization is **visibility-driven**. Snapshot APIs such as workspace create/fetch, folder lazy-load, file content reads, file mutations, and search are request/response flows and do **not** keep a backend filesystem watcher open. A live watcher exists only while at least one visible `FileExplorer.vue` consumer has acquired a live session for a workspace.
